\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. \cf0  All my heart this night rejoices,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj As I hear, far and near,
\par Sweetest angel voices;
\par 'Christ is born!' their choirs are singing,
\par Till the air, everywhere,
\par Now with joy is ringing.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Hark! a voice from yonder manger,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj Soft and sweet, doth entreat:
\par 'Flee from woe and danger;
\par Brethren, come: from all doth grieve you
\par You are freed; all you need
\par I will surely give you.'
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3.  Come, then, let us hasten yonder
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Here let all, great and small;
\par Kneel in awe and wonder.
\par Love Him who with love is yearning;
\par Hail the Start that, from far,
\par Bright with hope is burning.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li180\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4.  Thee, O Lord, with heed I'll cherish,
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0  Live to Thee, and with Thee
\par   'Dying, shall not perish,
\par  But shall dwell with Thee for ever
\par  Far on high, in the joy
\par \pard      That can alter never.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

